{
  "id": "ep101",
  "duration": 54.839,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 5.751,
      "text": "Panicked citizens in 1910 scrambled to buy gas masks and anti-comet pills.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Halley's Comet - May 29 1910.jpg",
        "credit": "Professor Edward Emerson Barnard at Yerkes Observatory, in Williams Bay, Wisconsin.",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Halley%27s_Comet_-_May_29_1910.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.751,
      "end": 12.021,
      "text": "The bizarre panic began when astronomers detected toxic cyanogen gas in a comet's tail.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Halley May 8.464 1910 Lowell.jpg",
        "credit": "Donn, Bertram; Rahe, Juergen; Brandt, John C.",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Halley_May_8.464_1910_Lowell.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.767,
          "end": 12.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.021,
      "end": 18.966,
      "text": "Sensationalized media reports quickly convinced the public that this toxic gas would wipe out all life.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Art Institute of Chicago (CC0)",
        "title": "The Great Halley's Comet",
        "credit": "Jos\u00e9 Guadalupe Posada\nMexican, 1852-1913",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/49276"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.033,
          "end": 18.967,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.966,
      "end": 26.386,
      "text": "The celestial culprit was Halley's Comet, a famous visitor returning every seventy-four to seventy-nine years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Comete Tapisserie Bayeux.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown authorUnknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Comete_Tapisserie_Bayeux.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.967,
          "end": 26.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 26.386,
      "end": 32.956,
      "text": "Even writer Mark Twain predicted his own death during this 1910 passage, passing away that April.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "MarkTwain.LOC.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown authorUnknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MarkTwain.LOC.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 26.4,
          "end": 28.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 28.9,
          "end": 32.967,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 32.956,
      "end": 40.201,
      "text": "But modern space probes revealed the terrifying toxic threat is actually a harmless, peanut-shaped ball of ice.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "International-Comet-Mission.png",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:International-Comet-Mission.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 32.967,
          "end": 40.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.201,
      "end": 47.526,
      "text": "Its giant fifteen-kilometer nucleus is blacker than coal, reflecting only about four percent of sunlight.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "International-Comet-Mission.png",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:International-Comet-Mission.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.2,
          "end": 47.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 47.526,
      "end": 54.489,
      "text": "This dark traveler safely returns around 2061, far too distant to make panicked citizens scramble.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Halley's Comet - May 29 1910.jpg",
        "credit": "Professor Edward Emerson Barnard at Yerkes Observatory, in Williams Bay, Wisconsin.",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Halley%27s_Comet_-_May_29_1910.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 47.533,
          "end": 54.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
